==Description==

The [[File:Cables_PartsLibrary.svg|24px]] [[Cables_PartsLibrary|Parts Library]] command is designed to perform operations on items in the local library.

The local library concerns elements: [[Cables_CableBox|CableBox]], [[Cables_CableConnector|CableConnector]], [[Cables_ElectricalDevice|ElectricalDevice]]. The [[Cables_PartsLibrary|Parts Library]] command allows for the creation of custom definitions for them. The local library is always stored on the user's computer and is independent of the document being edited. This means that the elements contained in a document sent to another computer are not automatically transferred to the local library at the new location. They exist only in the sent document.

The [[Cables_PartsLibrary|Parts Library]] command enables the creation of new items in the local library or deletion of existing items from local library depending on the context in which the command is invoked (see the [[#Usage|Usage]] and [[#Options|Options]] sections). Editing an item from a library is done by inserting the item into the current document, modifying it within that document, and then re-inserting it into the library under the same name.

The local library is automatically created in the {{incode|$FREECAD_USER_DIR/Cables/}} folder. The exact location of the {{incode|$FREECAD_USER_DIR}} can be checked in the [[Python_Console|Python Console]] by invoking the command: {{incode|FreeCAD.getUserAppDataDir()}}.

==Usage==

===Creating a new item in the local library===

Prerequisite: all the necessary components required to create an element in the library already exist within the current document and they are already correctly positioned relative to one another and to the main coordinate system. Refer to [[#Typical_workflow|Typical workflow]] or [[#Tutorials|Tutorials]] for more details.

# Select the solid object, or compound of solids. This could be, for example, a previously created object of type: [[Std_Part|Std Part]], [[PartDesign_Body|PartDesign Body]], [[Part_Compound| Part Compound]] etc., an object imported from STEP file or existing object from Cables Workbench. It will be the main shape of the new item in the library.
# If needed, select all necessary [[Cables_CableTerminal|CableTerminal]] objects holding the {{KEY|CTRL}} key. The order of selection is important. The CableTerminal objects will be numbered according to the order in which they are selected.
# If needed, select all necessary [[Cables_SnapLines|SnapLines]] objects holding the {{KEY|CTRL}} key. The order of selection is important. The SnapLines objects will be numbered according to the order in which they are selected.
# Run [[Cables_PartsLibrary|Parts Library]] command by one of these methods:
#* Press the {{Button|[[File:Cables_PartsLibrary.svg|24px]] [[Cables_PartsLibrary|Parts Library]]}} button.
#* Select the {{MenuCommand|Cables → [[File:Cables_PartsLibrary.svg|16px]] [[Cables_PartsLibrary|Parts Library]]}} option from the menu.
#* Right-click in the [[Tree_View|Tree View]] or the [[3D_View|3D View]] and select the {{MenuCommand|Cables → [[File:Cables_PartsLibrary.svg|16px]] [[Cables_PartsLibrary|Parts Library]]}} option from the context menu.
# The creation dialog box opens. See [[#Options|Options]] for more information. Select needed options and finally press the {{KEY|Add to local library}} button. If the element with '''Preset Full Name''' already exists in the library it will be overwritten upon further confirmation via the {{KEY|Force overwrite}} button.

===Removing items from the local library===

# Clear the selection of any objects (e.g. by clicking empty space in the [[3D_View|3D View]]).
# Run the [[Cables_PartsLibrary|Parts Library]] command as desribed in the step 4 above.
# The deletion dialog box opens. Select all items intended for removal and press the {{KEY|Delete}} button.

==Options==

* '''Element group''': Some of the following values may be available: , {{Value|Cable Box}}, {{Value|Cable Connector}}, {{Value|Electrical Device}} depending on the object that was selected before invoking the command.
* '''Class''': This is a conventional name that helps in classifying items within a library. This can be company name or widely used common name for group of connectors/devices, e.g. Molex, D-Sub, MCB
* '''Name''': This is a proper name identifying this item, e.g. a name provided by the manufacturer.
* '''Preset Full Name''': (read only) The unique name identifying an element within a library, constructed according to the following rule: Class_Name, where Class and Name are desribed above.
* '''Library STEP file''': This is a method for creating a STEP file in a library. Possible values are: {{Value|Copy from source STEP file}}, {{Value|Create from selected solid object}}. It is recommended to use {{Value|Copy from source STEP file}} whenever it is available, unless there is a need to regenerate the STEP file in accordance with the FreeCAD export rules.
* '''Source STEP file''': The full path name to the chosen STEP file if {{Value|Copy from source STEP file}} is selected above. It may be suggested automatically if it has been found in the local library.
* '''Ignore placement''': It forces the '''Placement''' property of the selected solid object to be ignored. It may be useful when we plan to recreate library elements from a received document. In such a case, they do not need to be manually positioned in their base location.
* '''Show details''': It shows the detailed list of items to create or modify as well as list of library files that will be created or modified.

==Notes==

* It is not possible to add or remove items from the built-in library. It is provided as-is, along with the entire [[Cables_Workbench|Cables Workbench]].
* It is possible to manually modify library files. The example tutorial about [[Cables_Create_Custom_Connector|creating custom connector]] written for previous versions of [[Cables_Workbench|Cables Workbench]] is still valid.

