==Typical workflow==

===Scenario 1: Making a new connector or device library part from a STEP file===
# Obtain the STEP file
#* Make your own shape of a connector/device and export it to the STEP file (example: [https://github.com/sargo-devel/Cables/blob/master/freecad/cables/resources/presets/lib/D-Sub_DE-9_M.FCStd D-Sub_DE-9_M])
#* or download a ready-made STEP file from the internet. Recommended format: AP242. '''VERY IMPORTANT''': Some STEP files may subsequently fail to load correctly from the library when creating new objects. Some STEP files might not load correctly from the library later on when creating new objects. The [[Cables_CableConnector#STEP_file|CableConnector STEP File]] describes how to deal with this problem.
# Create a new document
# Import the STEP file (command from menu: File/Import).
# Position the imported shape at the center of the coordinate system, in the orientation in which it is intended to be retrieved from the library later.
# Create a new "Connector_Dummy" and move it to the side so that it doesn't conflict with the imported shape (command [[Cables_CableConnector|CableConnector]]). This is needed to get [[Cables_CableTerminal|CableTerminal]] and [[Cables_SnapLines|SnapLines]] objects which can't be created directly.
# Delete the "CableConnector" object and answer "Yes" to the pop-up notification. There should remain three  '''CabeTerminal''' objects and one '''SnapLines''' object. They will be used to build a new library part.
# Move and rotate all needed Terminal objects into their target positions.
#* If there is an insufficient number of Terminal objects, they can be duplicated by copying and pasting.
#* Redundant Terminal objects can be deleted.
#* it is important that the #1 vertices of the Terminal objects are oriented outwards. This is needed when connecting the cables later on.
#* If necessary, the length of any Terminal object can be adjusted via its '''Length''' property.
# Set the '''Pin Name''' property for each Terminal object if needed.
# Move and rotate all needed SnapLines objects into their target positions. Follow the same rules as for the Terminal objects.
# Set the '''Snap Name''' property for each SnapLines object if needed.
# Follow the next steps according to [[#Creating_a_new_item_in_the_local_library|Creating a new item in the local library]].

===Scenario 2: Making a new parametric cable box library part===
# Create a new document
# Create a new "Customized" [[Cables_CableBox|CableBox]] by selecting "Customized" preset upon creation and set all needed box parameters.
# Select created CableBox object and follow the [[#Creating_a_new_item_in_the_local_library|Creating a new item in the local library]] without selecting any additional Terminal or SnapLines objects.
#* The dialog box will automatically propose the '''Class''' and '''Name'''. They can be changed if needed.

===Scenario 3: Making a new parametric terminal strip connector library part===
# Create a new document
# Create a new "Customized" [[Cables_CableConnector|CableConnector]] by selecting "Customized" preset upon creation and set all needed connector parameters.
# Select created CableConnector object and follow the [[#Creating_a_new_item_in_the_local_library|Creating a new item in the local library]] without selecting any additional Terminal or SnapLines objects.
#* The dialog box will automatically propose the '''Class''' and '''Name'''. They can be changed if needed.


